Template: homelab-drive/db_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PostgreSQL host to bootstrap this app's roles/schema on:
 Used only once, at first install, to run homelab-bootstrap-app-role.

Template: homelab-drive/pgbouncer_host
Type: string
Default: localhost
Description: PgBouncer host to register this app's runtime role with:
 Used only once, at first install. Also written into config.yml's
 database.host, so the running service connects through the pooler.

Template: homelab-drive/api_base
Type: string
Default: http://localhost:3000
Description: Base URL where homelab-api is reachable:
 Written into config.yml's homelab_api.base_url — every login and
 token check this app does goes through here.

Template: homelab-drive/listen_port
Type: string
Default: 2501
Description: Port for homelab-drive to listen on:

Template: homelab-drive/sso_base_url
Type: string
Default: http://127.0.0.1:2502
Description: Base URL where homelab-sso is reachable:
 Written into config.yml's sso.base_url. homelab-sso is the only place
 a user ever types a password -- this app redirects here for /login
 and /logout.

Template: homelab-drive/sso_redirect_uri
Type: string
Default: https://drive.test.mailmasker.org/oauth/callback
Description: This app's own OAuth callback URL:
 Must match exactly what's registered for the "drive" client in
 homelab-sso's own config (homelab-sso/drive_redirect_uri at that
 package's install time).

Template: homelab-drive/sso_client_secret
Type: password
Description: Shared secret for this app's "drive" OAuth client:
 Must match exactly what homelab-sso's own install printed for the
 "drive" client (dpkg-reconfigure homelab-sso to see it again, or
 rotate it). Unlike homelab-sso's own client secrets, there's no
 sensible default to auto-generate here -- this app is the consumer of
 a secret homelab-sso mints, not the minter.
